## Current repository integration cross-check (2026-10-11)

- Backend route: web-platform/backend/app/services/ai_adapter.py. When OPENROUTER_API_KEY is present, content planning uses only the explicit free OpenRouter model allowlist. Without the key, the route uses the deterministic mock adapter.
- The Groq → Cloudflare → Cohere → Gemini chain above is a proposed architecture from the live test notes, not an implemented provider chain for the backend content-plan route.
- The current route excludes the dynamic openrouter/free router and poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free until reproducibility/privacy acceptance is explicit. A model listed as free is not automatically suitable for unpublished content.
- Current integration-level unit coverage lives in web-platform/backend/tests/test_ai_adapter.py; manual live evidence is available through .github/workflows/openrouter-free-model-evidence.yml and requires a GitHub Actions secret. No live request is triggered by standard CI.
- The Voyage result in this report is for voyage-3-lite at 512 dimensions. Current RAG/database schema compatibility must be verified end-to-end; changing model IDs alone will not migrate existing vectors or fix dimension mismatches.
